WebCore: DocumentLoader.cpp includes EventLoop.h, whose type it uses

DocumentLoader.cpp calls eventLoop().queueTask() and never includes
EventLoop.h. Upstream builds get the declaration transitively, through
whichever source shares its unified-source bundle; which sources land
in a bundle depends on the feature flags, and ROCKNIX's option set
(packages/web/webkitgtk/package.mk) is not upstream's, so here
EventLoopTaskGroup is an incomplete type and WebCore stops compiling
(first met on 2.52.6 with the fork's cross gcc, object 8230 of 9097;
carried since, and applied on 2.54.0). Including what the file uses is
the fix upstream would take; no WebKit bug for it is recorded in the
fork yet (ROCKNIX fork, 2026-08-30).

--- a/Source/WebCore/loader/DocumentLoader.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/loader/DocumentLoader.cpp
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@
 #include "DocumentWriter.h"
 #include "ElementChildIteratorInlines.h"
 #include "Event.h"
+#include "EventLoop.h"
 #include "EventNames.h"
 #include "ExtensionStyleSheets.h"
 #include "FormSubmission.h"
